209 answers: 76 real ones, 133 broken on purpose.
Every negative is verified to no longer contain the fact it should.

  invented   a number that is not in the corpus at all
  neighbour  a real Meridian figure, from the wrong quarter

  no reference
    agreement with the label   44%
    Cohen's kappa              0.08
    wrong negatives passed     66 of 76
    neighbour negatives passed 52 of 57
    correct answers failed     0 of 76

  with the reference
    agreement with the label   100%
    Cohen's kappa              0.99
    wrong negatives passed     0 of 76
    neighbour negatives passed 1 of 57
    correct answers failed     0 of 76

Without the reference the judge let 118 of 133 wrong answers through.
With it, 1.

That is the difference between grading and guessing. A judge with no reference
is being asked whether an answer sounds right about a company it has never
heard of, and a confident sentence with a wrong number in it sounds exactly as
right as the true one.

Do not read the second row as 'judges work'. Read it as: this judge, on this
task, where correctness is a figure that either matches or does not. Every
negative here is checkable by comparing two strings, which is what the judge
did — and if that is your task, §22.8 has a cheaper suggestion than a model.
